# Shared Detection Schema — Module 1

Both vision/ and audio/ must output confidence scores in this shape,
so fusion/ can combine them without either side needing to know the
other's internals.

## Per-detection output (JSON)
{
  "image_id": "str",
  "visual_confidence": 0.0,
  "audio_confidence": 0.0,
  "occlusion_pct_actual": 0.0
}

## Notes
- visual_confidence: 0-1 float, from vision/ (YOLO detection confidence)
- audio_confidence: 0-1 float, from audio/ (tap-vs-noise classifier confidence)
  - defaults to 0.0 if no audio sample exists yet — lets vision/ be tested
    independently before audio/ is ready
- occlusion_pct_actual: 0-100 float, from vision/'s occlusion augmentation log
- fusion/combine_confidence.py takes visual_confidence + audio_confidence -> one fused scoremodule1_rgb_occlusion/audio/recordings/
